= Scope, controls and input identity
#text("These are recorded observations, not an evidence-review verdict. The scope is the fixed F11 model y²=x³+x+6, subgroup order 13, twelve nonidentity public bases and ten coordinate views. The views are covariance checks, not independent statistical samples. The 40 integer templates and eight control arms remain visible, including incomplete, failed and undefined outcomes. A false finite gate with integrity errors is not a mathematical counterexample. A finite gate result applies only to this registered template and fixture; no global ordering, novelty, complexity improvement, universal circuit obstruction or scientific status transition follows.")


#text("The validator-only truth-half positive control uses O(r) scalar enumeration. It tests the validator and retained-bit reduction; its zero predicate-evaluation count is not an executed candidate recovery. Actual fresh candidate recovery is reported from its separate trace stream. Failed public gates retain their not-attempted reasons and do not become successful recoveries.")


#text("Counter families are source-instrumented operations with separate setup, evaluation, public gate, fresh setup, fresh evaluation, reduction, census and validator work. No field/group price, prorating of global census/validator work, complete machine cost, qualified timing, memory measurement or attack speedup is inferred. Model/point scaling, Python container/control work, serialization, hashing, I/O and runtime/source checks include unmetered harness work. Candidate counters are not independently replayed. The full campaign includes the linear all-point gate and public census.")


